    "designNotes": "The roof has no reachable upper surface; it meets the top boundary. There is no intermediate floor refill between the launch and exit. Saved active ordinary full-jump and short-hop alternatives fail geometrically. The route uses three dashes from one initial charge by recovering once on the runway and once from the pod.",
    "endingForgiveness": "The final dash remains part of the continuous phrase. The low blade contact accepts a later cut; a four-frame later cycle start also completes. An earlier launch changes the later contact height and requires adaptation, so this remains a Fractured candidate.",
